 "goal": {
  "id": "37/G",
  "goal": "Explain how contextual inquiry can be used to gather usability requirements for an XR system by identifying user groups and challenges and converting findings into design guidelines and functional requirements.",
  "achieves": "It gives the learner a structured basis for deriving implementable XR system requirements from real user context in the system development life cycle."
 },
